  "text": "Beside its knobs, each module's card draws what it does, worked out from the same maths that makes the sound. The EQs — Parametric, Console and Program — draw their curve over your vocal as it plays: its spectrum before the EQ, dim, and after it, bright, with the peaks held for a moment. Each band has a dot on the curve: drag it to move the band's frequency and gain together, turn the mouse wheel over it for its width, double-click it to put the band back, or use the arrow keys. A whole drag is one step to undo. The De-esser draws the band it listens to and the cut it makes, and Trim its high-pass. The compressors, the Level Rider and the Limiter draw their curve — the level in against the level out — with a dot where your vocal sits on it now, and beneath it the gain reduction of the last four seconds. A steady note puts the dot on the curve; a sharp attack can lift it above for a moment, before the compressor catches it. Drag the threshold along the curve, or use the arrow keys: it turns the knob that sets it. The Gate's card shows the level it hears against its threshold, shaded where it is shut. The Delay draws its repeats on a timeline against your project's beat and bar, each"
